# Normalize every text file to LF, both in the repo and on checkout --
# regardless of a contributor's own core.autocrlf setting. Without this,
# a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true, Git's own Windows default)
# gets CRLF line endings in the working tree, and Prettier (which
# defaults to LF) then flags every single text file as unformatted --
# not a real issue, just working-tree noise that made a real 4-file CI
# failure impossible to distinguish from ~440 false positives when
# checked locally (see CONTRIBUTING.md's "Before you push" section).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets Git should never try to diff or normalize line endings
# for -- autodetection usually gets these right, but spelling them out
# removes any doubt.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.svg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
